[Desktop Entry]
Name=Suspend
Comment=Suspend to RAM
Exec=/usr/sbin/suspend
Icon=suspend.png
Terminal=false
Categories=Action;
# Categories=Action, NOT System, and that single word is what puts this
# entry where it belongs. Both consumers of this file special-case it:
#
#   * mb-applet-menu-launcher (applets/mb-applet-menu-launcher.c) tests
#     Categories for "Action" BEFORE it does any vfolder matching, and on
#     a hit sets m = mbmenu->rootmenu -- the top level of the menu,
#     alongside the Programs/System/Settings folders rather than inside
#     one of them. It also drops a separator above the first such entry
#     and passes MBMENU_NO_SORT, so the actions stay grouped at the root
#     instead of being alphabetised in among the folders.
#
#   * matchbox-desktop-classic (modules/dotdesktop.c) opens
#     add_a_dotdesktop_item() with "We dont want 'action' entrys" and
#     returns early on the same substring, so this stays off the desktop
#     icon view.
#
# With Categories=System these landed in the "System Tools" folder, one
# level down, which is not where a power action should live.
#
# There is also deliberately no Type= line. That is now belt-and-braces
# rather than the mechanism -- dotdesktop.c's Action check fires before
# it ever looks at Type -- but it costs nothing and independently keeps
# the entry off the desktop, which gates on Type being exactly
# "Application". Do NOT reach for Type=PanelApp: the menu-launcher
# special-cases that exact string LAST, after the Action branch, and
# would redirect this into its "Utilities/Panel" applet submenu.
